From: Project Luma <luma@projectluma.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: fix CSID 3.4.0 PHY3 selection

The TFE CSID665 receiver used by SM7635 encodes the selected CSIPHY in
bits 22:20 of CSI2_RX_CFG0.  PHY indices are biased by one, so CSIPHY3 must
be written as value 4.  The existing two-bit mask silently truncates that
value to zero and prevents sensors connected to CSIPHY3 from reaching the
CSID receiver.

Qualcomm's downstream CSID665 definition exposes the same field with mask
0x7.  Widen the mainline field accordingly.  Existing PHY0 through PHY2
encodings are unchanged.

---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
index 2fa43fc97b41..ce62abb55e89 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #define CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG0					(0x100)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_NUM_ACTIVE_LANES_MASK	GENMASK(1, 0)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_DLX_INPUT_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(17, 4)
-#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(21, 20)
+#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(22, 20)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_BASE_IDX	1
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_TYPE_SEL		BIT(24)
 
-- 
2.51.0
